                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/1278a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-27T13:00:00-05:00">December 27, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. Please tell Aranha that I would greatly appreciate it if he would let you
                    know for my information what results may have been obtained by Dr. Mello Franco
                    in Lima in connection with the Peruvian-Ecuadoran boundary dispute. If it were
                    possible for Dr. Mello Franco before he leaves to obtain some agreement in
                    principle between the Peruvian and Ecuadoran Foreign Ministers it would be an
                    achievement of the utmost significance and would provide, I believe, a
                    satisfactory and rapid method for a definitive settlement of the dispute. Please
                    telegraph such information as you may obtain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
